    {
      "text": "When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own, John 8:44. say, I know him not, I shall be a liar, John 8:55. why hath Satan filled thine heart to lie to the Holy Ghost, Acts 5:3. thou hast not lied unto men, but unto God, Acts 5:4 (Alma 12:3). changed the truth of God into a lie, Rom. 1:25. putting away lying, speak every man truth, Eph. 4:25. Lie not one to another, Col. 3:9. Speaking lies in hypocrisy, 1 Tim. 4:2. eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised, Titus 1:2. Cretians are alway liars, Titus 1:12. impossible for God to lie, Heb. 6:18. say that we have not sinned, we make him a liar, 1 Jn. 1:10. saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, 1 Jn. 2:4. no lie is of the truth, 1 Jn. 2:21. Who is a liar but he that denieth that Jesus is the Christ, 1 Jn. 2:22. say, I love God, and hateth his brother, he is a liar, 1 Jn. 4:20. he that believeth not God hath made him a liar, 1 Jn. 5:10. all liars, shall have their part in the lake, Rev. 21:8. whosoever loveth and maketh a lie, Rev. 22:15.",
